1
00:00:00,211 --> 00:00:02,881
(Raj:)That's a
lot less big.

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:07,550
(Colonel Williams:)Yes, it's...
this much less big.

3
00:00:07,552 --> 00:00:10,022
(Howard:)I'm not even sure
that's possible.

4
00:00:10,021 --> 00:00:12,191
(Colonel Williams:)Well, I ran it
by some colleagues at MIT,

5
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:14,860
(Colonel Williams:)and they thought they could
get it done in four months.

6
00:00:14,859 --> 00:00:15,969
(Howard:)Four months?

7
00:00:15,994 --> 00:00:17,864
(Sheldon:)Yeah, we'll do it
in two!

8
00:00:17,862 --> 00:00:19,832
(Sheldon:)Hi. I'm Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

9
00:00:19,831 --> 00:00:21,901
(Sheldon:)I'm the actual brains
behind this project.

10
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:23,899
(Sheldon:)Also, engineers aren't
real scientists,

11
00:00:23,901 --> 00:00:25,431
(Sheldon:)MIT's a trade school,

12
00:00:25,436 --> 00:00:28,706
(Sheldon:)and the Death Star is
from Star Wars, not Star Trek!

13
00:00:28,706 --> 00:00:30,836
(Sheldon:)But otherwise,

14
00:00:30,842 --> 00:00:33,742
(Sheldon:)thank you for your service.

15
00:00:38,082 --> 00:00:39,812
(Sheldon:)Hi.

16
00:00:39,817 --> 00:00:42,857
(Amy:)Howard told me you were working
late, so I brought dinner.

17
00:00:42,854 --> 00:00:45,654
(Bernadette:)Oh, thanks. You know, I just
wanted to get some work done

18
00:00:45,656 --> 00:00:46,826
(Bernadette:)without people
congratulating me

19
00:00:46,824 --> 00:00:48,224
(Bernadette:)about the baby
every five minutes.

20
00:00:48,226 --> 00:00:49,826
(Amy:)I spent my day
alone in the lab

21
00:00:49,827 --> 00:00:52,597
(Amy:)waiting for a rat
to die of anthrax.

22
00:00:52,597 --> 00:00:56,027
(Bernadette:)Did you come here
to bring me dinner or to gloat?

23
00:00:56,033 --> 00:00:59,373
(Amy:)Well, I came to see
how you were feeling,

